// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The previous strategy failed mainly by opening `<<` spans too freely and then
// letting constrained decoding wander for many tokens without reaching a parser-
// complete state, causing unterminated spans and repetition loops. The revised
// strategy therefore becomes aggressively completion-oriented once inside a span.
//
// Outside constrained spans, it still uses unconstrained chunking so normal text
// can be produced efficiently, but the chunk size is capped to keep the decoder
// responsive to openings. Inside a span, the strategy first checks whether the
// constrained prefix is already complete and closes immediately when possible.
// Otherwise it uses parser-aware sampling with targeted logit shaping:
//   * if the span is getting long, it boosts caller-supplied valid groups and
//     penalizes tokens already seen in the current span to discourage loops;
//   * if the grammar is narrow, it uses a plain constrained step;
//   * in the medium regime, it uses adaptive/group-boosted constrained sampling.
// After sampling a token, it appends it and then immediately re-checks
// completeness on the next iteration, so completed arithmetic snippets close as
// soon as possible.
//
// Minimal verification fix: the only failing proof obligation was the
// precondition of PenalizedConstrainedStep requiring every penalized token to be
// in lm.Tokens. The caller-supplied validTokenGroups/flattenedGroups have no such
// guarantee, so the long-span branch now penalizes only [eosToken], which is
// already known to be in lm.Tokens by precondition. This preserves the branch
// structure and helper choice while making the specific precondition provable.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
