// if the arithmetic span is complete, it closes with ">>"; otherwise it uses an
// adaptive constrained sampler that boosts caller-provided token groups when the
// grammar is narrow. If recent arithmetic context is non-empty, it additionally
// boosts tokens that intersect that context before masked constrained sampling.
// This is intended to keep arithmetic computations syntactically valid while
// softly preferring locally relevant digits/operators and any caller-specified
// preferred token groups.
