// language reasoning. When the model emits `<<`, we enter constrained mode and
// require every subsequent token to remain parser-valid for the arithmetic
// sublanguage. If the constrained prefix is already complete, we immediately
// close it with `>>`. Otherwise we choose the next arithmetic token with an
// adaptive constrained helper that boosts provided token groups only when the
// parser-valid frontier is narrow.
//
// This supports the task because all arithmetic computations are forced to live
// inside parser-valid spans, while the surrounding explanation remains fluent.
// The delimiter state ensures `currentConstrainedOut` contains only the content
// between delimiters, which is exactly the prefix the parser validates.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
